# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. Checked out with CRLF on Windows and
# committed that way, bash on the CI runner fails with "\r: command not found".
*.sh text eol=lf

# The git hooks are shell scripts too -- they just have no extension, so the
# rule above misses them. Same failure, and it would bite on this machine
# rather than on CI: a CRLF hook aborts every commit.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# The README screenshots. git detects binary content on its own, so this is
# belt-and-braces -- but core.autocrlf is on here, and a PNG that ever gets
# treated as text comes out of a checkout corrupted.
*.png binary